{{- /* internal/render/templates/code.gohtml — one colorized code
excerpt (§6): htmlCodeView.Spans() (html_highlight.go) already tokenized
and merged the excerpt into htmlCodeSpans, so this template only ranges
over them — a token whose class is "" (§6.2's plain-text fallback: Text,
Whitespace, Background, Error, Other, and anything else outside the six
named categories) writes its Value straight into the <pre> as escaped
text with no wrapping <span> at all; every other token gets one
<span class="c-*">. htmlCodeView.Label() (§6.3) is the file's own
extension read off the owning anchor — never chroma's lexer name, which
is never called here — and renders as a small tag ahead of the block
only when non-empty; with no anchor to read one from, Label is "" and no
label element renders at all. overflow-x: auto and white-space: pre on
the <pre> itself (§7.5, code.css) keep a long line scrolling within its
own block rather than widening the page. Nothing here touches Value
through anything but ordinary {{ }} text-content escaping — the same
contextual autoescaping every other field on this page already goes
through (§4).

Bead .4 owns this file's content. Dot is htmlCodeView
(internal/render/html_view_finding.go). */ -}}
{{define "code"}}
{{if .Label}}<div class="code-lang">{{.Label}}</div>{{end}}<pre class="code-block"><code>{{range .Spans}}{{if .Class}}<span class="{{.Class}}">{{.Text}}</span>{{else}}{{.Text}}{{end}}{{end}}</code></pre>
{{end}}
